n act upon  should you so desire  and then the next slide as you say isn't  just for you  you can actually share it with your  physician and we think some of the data  that you get from your wearable is even  more accurate than what you'll get in  the doctor's office  and ultimately what i'd like to do is  see all these technologies brought  into healthcare and be able to better  manage people's health so  i'm a believer people will be getting  their genome sequence before they're  born  and then together with a more detailed  biochemical measurement so the so-called  omic measurements  and and sensor information we can better  manage people's health we can predict  disease risk better  catch disease early and again hopefully  manage  things so we can shift from sick care to  health care  really try and keep people healthier for  a much much longer time  i happen to have a very very amazing lab  that's shown here  so these folks in my lab are listening  to the left i won't have time to go  through all of them but when you shall  uh brian penning kevin contraposis uh  sofia rose i don't see her listed there  they were all very very powerful  in helping getting and studying started  and going we have amazing collaborators  george weinstock  uh helped very fantastic for the  microbiome work  tracy mclaughlin on the clinical side uh  people who built some of the personal  health dashboard to listen to the right  amir in particular and rush i wanted to  shout out to them expose them by the  team down below  and it's just been an amazing group of  people coming together to try and  transform the way we  currently do healthcare so thanks again  for having me here  uh happy to take any questions online  thank you dr snyder for the outstanding  presentation  for additional informative presentations  view our agenda  on our events page as a final reminder  our speaker will follow up with any  questions you have submitted  via email thank you again for your  participation
 

